decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-07-21-766
    decision: 'Universal cold-agent usability: agents of ALL providers must use Warpline as easily as git. Pre-registered as falsifier F4 (cold-agent legibility) with thresholds; standing hard stop on all surface work while F4 is unmeasured.'
    rationale: Git is easy for agents because it is MEMORIZED in model weights, not because it is well designed. Moat-silence plus no-publishing means Warpline will never enter any model's weights, so every agent encounter is permanently a COLD encounter and runtime self-description is the only available mechanism.
  - id: PANEL-2026-07-21-priority
    decision: Next move is the first contested verdict (fork two agents, shared symbol, sequential admit), ahead of SP2 skins, over-block stage 2, and the MCP server.
    rationale: Unanimous across 5 rankers, with 3 of 5 ranking their own authored lane below it. The adjudication path has never executed; every other candidate refines an unexercised claim. Jinx predicted the panel would pick SP2 and named the disconfirming experiment as the one he expected them to avoid.
learnings:
  - 'The empty denominator was a ROUTING fact, not a workflow problem: no scratch ref had ever been written, so base equaled selvage and the KNOT branch was structurally unreachable. Verify the mechanism before proposing a process change.'
  - A refusal path can be 0-for-N by conjunct construction rather than by rarity — pick.ts:208's second and third conjuncts are mutually exclusive across all recorded history.
  - 'Builder self-reported test counts must be independently re-run: 609/609 reported vs 608/609 actual, and diagnosing the delta required a stashed baseline re-run.'
  - Panel rankings are more trustworthy when each ranker is explicitly asked to rank against their own authored lane; three of five did so here, and the unanimous winner was the option its own predictor expected to be avoided.
