body: |-
  ## The finding that reframed the arc

  Four of eight panelists independently concluded the repo has never produced a contested verdict. Coordinator verification found the cause is STRUCTURAL, not behavioral — correcting an earlier reading ("one human editing serially") that implied a workflow overhaul:

  - `.warpline/refs/scratch/` has NEVER been written (dir mtime Jun 25).
  - `admit.ts:383` — `readScratch(root, opts.agentId) ?? readSelvage(wdir)` → with no scratch, base ≡ selvage ALWAYS.
  - `admit.ts:128` — `if (selvage.stateId === base.stateId) return FAST_ADMIT`.
  - Therefore `admit.ts:132-153` — the ONLY producer of KNOT/DANGLE/CLEAN — is unreachable on the exercised path. 21/21 verdicts (12 FAST_ADMIT, 9 NOOP) are forced by construction.

  Second, independently found by Jinx and verified: `pick.ts:208` refuses on `gateReal && !row.wouldSeal && row.status !== 'NOOP'`. Across all 21 rows `wouldSeal:false` occurs on exactly 9 — ALL of them NOOP. Zero rows satisfy both conjuncts. **The refusal path is 0-for-21.** Related: `pick.ts:136` computes `gateReal` but `pick.ts:140` passes `agentId ?? 'auto-seal'` only into the telemetry row, so `gate.agentWrites:"real"` has never actually been consulted — no row carries `gate:"real"`.

  Consequence: F1, F2, F4, organic K3 and the false-KNOT rate all have denominator zero, and K3's linked/independent arms are both 0 (`grades.jsonl` = 7 rows, all `priorClass:"pick"`).

  ## The gate ruling

  Loid audited her own machinery and reported against it: 200/200 debates `complementary` with ZERO contradictory; 96/96 nominations `surfaced:false`; 11/11 settlements `journalsWritten:0` with `chainLive:true`; 5 certifications, 0 overturns. Verdict: "a gate that has never once returned false is not a gate." The F3 drill that DID fail was a mechanical byte check with no agent in the loop. Ruling adopted: falsifiers gate, the team is the instrument that tries to trip them, the founder holds the decision.

  ## What was built

  `refusal:v1` (SP0+SP1, commit 969a32c6) — schemaVersion, code, verdict, gate, retriable, contested[] capped at 32 + contestedTotal, pointers, `next[]` (verb/params/requires/principal — the F4-critical field), override. `refuse()` is the single constructor. Scope ruled by Arky: Knot.rule IN, rankVerdicts IN, schemaVersion IN, over-block signal OUT (uncalibrated at n=3), scrutiny OUT (it is the permission model; refusal is merely its report surface).

  Over-block stage 1 (commit 47f55ec9) — Trace rejected all three filed options and found a fourth. BRUSH demotion was DISQUALIFIED: its only available predicate is shared verbatim with the 12 real TRUE-INTERFERENCE catches. The chosen fix carries a signature-only projection as an essence-neutral field, since `normalizedContract` (essence-hash.ts:89-110) does not hash `codeSignature`. Proven not asserted: `signature-projection.test.ts` pins GOLDEN_STATE_ID and per-symbol GOLDEN_CONTENT_IDS.

  ## Honest state

  Both are inert. `refusal:v1` is UNREACHABLE — `exitCodeFor` exported and unconsumed, CLI still prose-behind-exit-1, daemon untouched; F4 has not improved by one point. Stage 1 changed NO verdict; the false-KNOT still fires 3/3. Also discovered: `dist/cli.js` was 4 days stale, so the live post-commit shadow gate had been grading commits with Jul-17 code (rebuilt).

  ## Verification discipline that paid

  Kit reported 609/609. The actual full-suite result was 608/609. The failure was benign (parallel-load contention in absorb-concurrency: 19.32s with changes vs 22.14s on a stashed baseline re-run at 539/539), but the report was wrong and would have shipped a false green. Jinx also caught the coordinator citing 19 shadow rows when the live file held 21.
